  "escudoActivoPor": "{nombre} activated the Security Shield",
  "@escudoActivoPor": {
    "placeholders": { "nombre": { "type": "String" } }
  },
  "escudoPaso0Titulo": "What is the Security Shield?",
  "escudoPaso0Desc": "It's a set of protection measures that activate when both users of a deal accept them. Its goal is to prevent fraud and ensure the meeting is safe.\n\nWho should activate it?\nBoth users of the deal must accept the Shield. If one activates it, the other receives a notification to accept or reject it. If the second user rejects it, the chat will close for both.",
  "escudoPaso1Titulo": "What happens when the Shield is active?",
  "escudoPaso1Desc": "3.1. Link and phone blocking: The app automatically detects and blocks phone numbers and external links in messages. This prevents sharing contact info outside the platform and reduces the risk of scams.",
  "escudoPaso2Titulo": "How to close the deal",
  "escudoPaso2Desc": "To close the deal, first propose a meeting: tap the shield in the chat's top bar and choose \"Propose meeting\". There you select province, canton, district, a safe place and the date with time. Send the proposal and the other user receives it as a card in the chat. When they accept, the meeting is scheduled but the chat stays open: you can keep talking. To close the deal, tap the shield again and choose \"Close deal\". A confirmation dialog opens. When both confirm, the chat is blocked and protections activate.",
  "escudoPaso3Titulo": "Attendance confirmation",
  "escudoPaso3Desc": "One hour before the meeting, both users will receive a notification to confirm their attendance. If either doesn't confirm within 15 minutes after the notification, the other user can cancel the meeting up to 15 minutes before the agreed time.",
  "escudoPaso4Titulo": "GPS tracking",
  "escudoPaso4Desc": "3.3. GPS tracking on the day of the meeting: On the agreed day, 15 minutes before the meeting time, both users must be at the place and activate GPS to verify their location. If 5 minutes before the agreed time the user hasn't activated GPS and hasn't verified their identity, it will be considered late. If 15 minutes after the agreed time the user hasn't done so, it will be considered a no-show. In both cases, it's recorded and can be sanctioned according to MiMarketplace rules.",
  "escudoPaso5Titulo": "Facial verification",
  "escudoPaso5Desc": "3.4. Identity verification before chat: To unlock the meeting chat, both users must confirm they are who they say they are. This is enabled 15 minutes before the agreed time and is a mandatory requirement to open the chat. The system will ask each one to take a photo on the spot. Then, the other user must compare that photo with the profile photo to confirm they match. It's important to pay attention, because verification is enabled when the other user activates it, and you must follow the instructions on screen. This prevents someone else from using the account.",
  "escudoPaso6Titulo": "Additional considerations",
  "escudoPaso6Desc": "4.1. Voluntary cancellation: Any user can cancel their attendance to the meeting as long as more than one hour remains before the agreed time. Once less than one hour remains, cancellation is no longer available.\n\nHow to cancel? Enter the item chat, tap the shield button in the top bar and choose \"Cancel deal\". A dialog opens showing the meeting date and telling you if you can still cancel or if less than an hour remains. If possible, confirm and the meeting is canceled for both.\n\nAlways check the Alerts section. Meeting reminders, attendance confirmation, identity verification and any status changes arrive there. You must check them often so you don't miss anything important.",
